    "post_decision_tracking": "Atlas Crossing Partners Fund I exit IC memo recommending the sale of Meridian Safety Systems, Inc. to Honeywell Safety Products for $268M enterprise value (9.4x LTM Adj. EBITDA of $28.4M). The transaction is an all-cash stock purchase with a target close of April 15, 2018. ACP invested $42M total equity (Oct 2012 platform + 3 bolt-ons) and realized gross proceeds of ~$141.8M, generating 2.8x gross MOIC and ~22.4% gross IRR over a 5.5-year hold. The investment exceeded its base-case underwrite of 2.5x MOIC. Value creation was driven by organic growth (43%), bolt-on acquisitions (31%), multiple expansion from 6.6x to 9.4x (23%), and FCF/debt paydown (3%). Three bolt-ons (Central States Safety Supply, Appalachian PPE Distributors, Gulf Coast Safety Group) were fully integrated. Revenue grew from $72M to $198M and EBITDA from $9.0M to $28.4M over the hold period."
